# F4W Online credentials — template. Copy it, don't edit it in place:
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# Then fill both values into .env. Both must be set, or the pair is ignored
# and you are prompted for your login interactively instead.
#
# Nothing auto-loads .env — there is no python-dotenv dependency — so source
# it yourself first:
#
#     set -a; . ./.env; set +a
#     f4w-download --all --watch
#
# That sources the file as a shell script, so wrap the password in single
# quotes if it contains spaces or any of $ # " \ ` — otherwise the shell
# eats them and the login fails for no visible reason:
#
#     F4W_PASSWORD='my $ecret pa55word'
#
# .env is gitignored. This file is not, so keep real credentials out of it.

F4W_USERNAME=
F4W_PASSWORD=
